From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0187-shared-romfs-fillers.patch

Source: 0187-shared-romfs-fillers.patch
Core patch: tools/eglantine-patches, next free number after 0181 (0187 if in order).

The 106,496-block site, "df136 de734 2df087 2d40a3 84d564 431645", is make_shared<StaticVfsFile> in
ConcatenatedVfsFile::MakeConcatenatedFile from CreateRomFS from AppLoader_NUP::ReadRomFS: one object for
the padding of up to 15 bytes after most of the RomFS's 186,587 files. A filler of one length is the same
read-only file, so there is one of each length now, and the map is made to its size instead of doubling
past it (8.5 MiB for 6.8). Saves about 10 MiB and 110,000 blocks. Reads do not change, so no switch.

Host check: 20,000 files with 6,236 gaps, one whole read and 200,000 random reads, old and new code
give the expected bytes. Not compiled for the console.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/core/file_sys/vfs/vfs_concat.cpp b/src/core/file_sys/vfs/vfs_concat.cpp
index b5cc9a9e91..36136307db 100644
--- a/src/core/file_sys/vfs/vfs_concat.cpp
+++ b/src/core/file_sys/vfs/vfs_concat.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <map>
 #include <utility>
 
 #include "common/assert.h"
@@ -72,7 +73,17 @@ VirtualFile ConcatenatedVfsFile::MakeConcatenatedFile(
     // Make the concatenation map from the input.
     std::vector<ConcatenationEntry> concatenation_map;
 
-    concatenation_map.reserve(files.size());
+    // A built RomFS has a gap of up to 15 bytes after most files, and a filler of each length is
+    // the same read-only file: a game of 186,587 files held about 110,000 of them, one heap block each
+    // (run 61). The map is made to size: doubling it left 8.5 MiB for 7.
+    std::size_t gaps = 0;
+    u64 next_offset = 0;
+    for (const auto& [offset, file] : files) {
+        gaps += offset > next_offset ? 1 : 0;
+        next_offset = offset + file->GetSize();
+    }
+    concatenation_map.reserve(files.size() + gaps);
+    std::map<u64, VirtualFile> fillers;
     u64 last_offset = 0;
 
     // Iteration of a multimap is ordered, so offset will be strictly non-decreasing.
@@ -80,9 +91,13 @@ VirtualFile ConcatenatedVfsFile::MakeConcatenatedFile(
         const auto size = file->GetSize();
 
         if (offset > last_offset) {
+            VirtualFile& filler = fillers[offset - last_offset];
+            if (filler == nullptr) {
+                filler = std::make_shared<StaticVfsFile>(filler_byte, offset - last_offset);
+            }
             concatenation_map.emplace_back(ConcatenationEntry{
                 .offset = last_offset,
-                .file = std::make_shared<StaticVfsFile>(filler_byte, offset - last_offset),
+                .file = filler,
             });
         }
 
